# utf8_u32_roundtrip.tkr — the SM-STRU32 codec fixture. `main.tks` builds a byte string mixing
# ASCII, 2/3-byte BMP characters, and a 4-byte astral character, decodes it to `[]u32` codepoints
# via `teko::text::decode_utf8_u32`, re-encodes via `teko::text::encode_u32_utf8`, and exits 0
# only if the round-tripped bytes match the original byte-for-byte.

Feature: utf8_u32_roundtrip — decode_utf8_u32/encode_u32_utf8 round-trip mixed-width UTF-8 text

  Scenario: roundtrip_ascii_bmp_astral_bytes_matches_original
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
